The game finishes.
We take our bags.
I walk to the front desk.
I am going to return the rented racket.
The clerk is standing there.
I give that racket to him.
"Did you like the game?" he asks me.
"Yes, I liked it very much," I reply.
"The courts here are very good."
"I like to come here every Thursday."
"Did you play well?" he asks.
"Yes, I played well," I say with a smile.
"I can come next Thursday too."
"You must certainly come," he says happily.
I say thank you to him.
Then I walk towards my friends.
